{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Two little boys had two little toys
Each had a [G7]wooden [C]horse
Gaily they played, on [G]a summer’s day
[A]Warriors both of [D]course
One [G]little chap then had a mishap
Broke off his [G7]horse's [C]head
Wept for his toy, [G]but cried with joy
When [A]he heard his [D]brother [G]say:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 1}
"Did [G]you think I would [C]leave you [G]crying
When there's room on my [G7]horse for [C]two?
Climb up here, Jack, and stop your [G]crying
We’ll [A]mend up your horse with [D]glue
When we [G]grow up, we'll [C]both be [G]soldiers
And our horses will [G7]not be [C]toys
And maybe you will [G]remember
When [A]we were [D]two little [G]boys"
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Long years passed, war came at last
Bravely they [G7]marched [C]away
Cannon roared loud, [G]midst that wild crowd
Where [A]wounded and dying Joe [D]lay
[G]Then came a cry, a rider dashed by
Out from the [G7]ranks of [C]blue
Galloped away to [G]where Joe lay
When [A]he heard his [D]brother [G]say:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
"Did [G]you think I would [C]leave you [G]dying
When there's room on my [G7]horse for [C]two?
Climb up here, Jack, we'll soon be [G]flying
To the [A]ranks of the boys in [D]blue
Can’t [G]you see Jack, [C]I'm all [G]a-tremble?
It may be the [G7]flash and the [C]noise
Or it may be because I [G]remember
When [A]we were [D]two little [G]boys"
{end_of_chorus}
